{{Term/Store|Baked Apple|Baked Apples|Series, BotW, TotK|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="Inventory"/><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Baked Apple}}<br/>Direct heat has softened and sweetened this apple. Eat it to restore three-quarters of a heart.|Inventory|TotK}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Baked Apples are a type of [[Roasted Food]] that results from [[Apple]]s making contact with [[Fire]] or a [[Scorching Climate]].<ref name="Inventory"/><ref>{{Cite|An apple and an open flame make for a succulent treat.|Old Man|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Simple foods such as apples are fine to eat raw, but roasting them on a fire makes them tastier and more nutritious.|Old Man|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Guide|BotW Piggyback|page= 295}}</ref> They are softer and sweeter than regular Apples.<ref name="Inventory"/> By eating one, [[Link]] can heal three quarters of a [[Heart]] to his [[Life Gauge]].<ref name="Inventory"/>

When Link first meets the [[Old Man]] at his [[Campfire]], he can steal his Baked Apple and have the Old Man lecture him.<ref>{{Cite|I BEG YOUR PARDON! I do believe that is my baked apple! You can't just go about taking whatever you please!|Old Man|BotW}}</ref> The Old Man will then tell Link he was only teasing him, and he welcomes him to help himself to his Baked Apples.<ref>{{Cite|Oho ho! Forgive me—I could not resist pulling your leg. Please help yourself.|Old Man|BotW}}</ref>

If Link speaks to [[Juney]], who can be found in [[Rito Village]], she will explain that she is upset with her husband, [[Jogo]], for bringing her there for her honeymoon, and they only way she will not divorce him is if he brings her a Baked Apple.<ref>{{Cite|He already apologized, but if he doesn't want a divorce, I told him he'd better bring me a {{Color BotW|Blue|baked apple}}.|Juney|BotW}}</ref> This initiates "[[The Apple of My Eye]]" [[Side Quest]]. Returning to Juney with a Baked Apple in Link's [[Inventory]] will be able to smell it.<ref>{{Cite|*sniff sniff*<br/>I know that smell!<br/>You've got a {{Color BotW|Blue|baked apple}}!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> She then asks if she can have one, promising a present for Link in return.<ref name="One">{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|one}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> If Link decides to give her one, she rewards him with a [[Silver Rupee]].<ref>{{Cite|[Sure thing.] You serious? Cheers! Just hold out your hand.|Juney|BotW}}</ref> Juney laments that her husband does not Cook Baked Apples for her very often.<ref>{{Cite|Now if I could only get my husband to cook me a {{Color BotW|Blue|baked apple}} every once in a while.|Juney|BotW}}</ref> She also asks Link to bring her more Baked Apples if he can.<ref>{{Cite|I've got a second stomach and a hollow leg for {{Color BotW|Blue|baked apples}}. Bring me as many as you possibly can.|Juney|BotW}}</ref>

When Link brings Baked Apples to Juney, she will pay a greater amount per Apple depending on how many are available.<ref>{{Cite|The more you bring me, the more I'll pay you for each one.|Juney|BotW}}</ref> She buys Baked Apples in groups of one,<ref name="One"/> five,<ref>{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|five}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> 10,<ref>{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|10}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> 30,<ref>{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|30}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> 50,<ref>{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|50}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref> and 100.<ref>{{Cite|Can I have {{Color BotW|Blue|100}}? I'll give you a present!|Juney|BotW}}</ref>

